WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.266
This study explores the Formula One hybrid architecture used from twenty fourteen through twenty twenty five.

00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:10.750
A small V six engine works alongside two motor generators and an energy store.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.809
The detailed exterior depicts the twenty twenty three Red Bull car, modeled by Redgrund.

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:17.936
The internal assembly is educational.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.661
Lift the bodywork to expose the power unit.

00:00:22.661 --> 00:00:27.860
The engine, turbocharger, electrical machines and battery form an integrated system.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.646
Their exact packaging varies by manufacturer.

00:00:30.646 --> 00:00:36.897
The separation shown here is an editorial animation, not a physical explosion or a service procedure.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.310
Six cylinders, arranged in a ninety degree V, displace one point six litres.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.181
Combustion drives the crankshaft.

00:00:46.181 --> 00:00:51.909
The reconstructed housings, carbon intake and insulated exhausts follow published Honda engine views.

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:56.503
Open the web cutaway to run six pistons and their connecting rods in slow motion.

00:00:56.503 --> 00:00:58.998
The dimensions and phasing are illustrative.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.049
The exhaust turbine drives a shaft shared with the compressor and the heat motor generator.

00:01:05.049 --> 00:01:07.879
The generator converts shaft work into electricity.

00:01:07.879 --> 00:01:11.763
In motor mode it helps accelerate the compressor and reduce turbo lag.

00:01:11.763 --> 00:01:14.592
It does not directly convert heat into electricity.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.989
The kinetic motor generator couples to the crankshaft.

00:01:22.989 --> 00:01:27.031
It recovers energy under braking and supplies torque during acceleration.

00:01:27.031 --> 00:01:30.574
In this era its power limit is one hundred and twenty kilowatts.

00:01:30.574 --> 00:01:36.719
The energy routes have separate limits: two megajoules to the store and four megajoules from the store per lap.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.722
The battery buffers energy while control electronics manage charging and deployment.

00:01:44.722 --> 00:01:51.073
Four megajoules divided by one hundred and twenty kilowatts gives thirty three point three seconds before losses.

00:01:51.073 --> 00:01:53.378
Direct heat generator supply is separate.

00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:58.999
For twenty twenty six, the heat generator was removed and maximum kinetic generator power increased.

